NB-QU-01 a full queue refuses at once, the refused go to dead letters in order, the queue keeps the first -> new: n=0 has=false | a: n=1 has=true | b: n=2 has=true | c: n=3 has=true | d: n=3 has=true | e: n=3 has=true | dead=[d<-snd->recv, e<-snd->recv] | drain=[a, b, c] n=0 has=false
NB-QU-02 dequeue frees a slot: the next enqueue is accepted and the order is still first in first out -> first=a rest=[b, d] dead=[c<-recv->recv, e<-recv->recv] n=0 has=false
NB-QU-03 capacity 1 keeps one; capacity 0 is a valid queue that refuses everything -> one: n=1 has=true drain=[a] dead=[b<-recv->recv, c<-recv->recv] | zero: n=0 has=false drain=[] dead=[x<-other->other, y<-other->other]
NB-QU-04 the dead letter carries the message, the envelope's sender and the receiver; a DeadLetter message is not dropped -> dead=[refused<-snd->recv, noSender<-deadLetters->recv, DeadLetter(inner)<-snd->recv] queue=[kept]
NB-QU-05 cleanUp moves a full queue to the target in order and frees every slot -> source=n=0 has=false target=n=3 has=true order=[a, b, c] | refilled: n=3 has=true drain=[e, f, g] dead=[d<-recv->recv, h<-recv->recv]
NB-QC-01 four producers, nobody dequeues: exactly capacity accepted, every other message dead-lettered -> accepted=10 dead=190 acceptedOrdered=true deadOrdered=true everyMessageAccountedOnce=true
NB-QC-02 four producers and one consumer: every message is received or dead-lettered exactly once, per-producer order, never above capacity -> everyMessageAccountedOnce=true receivedOrdered=true neverAboveCapacity=true n=0 has=false
